\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24\b Project Report: Personalized Shopping Journey Agent System\b0\par
\par
\b 1. Project Overview\b0\par
This project implements a multi-agent AI system designed to provide a personalized, high-end shopping experience while strictly adhering to modern privacy standards (GDPR/CCPA). The system acts as a "Digital Personal Shopper" that understands user style, budget, and dislikes while acting as a protective barrier for their personal data.\par
\par
\b 2. System Architecture\b0\par
The system follows a modular orchestration pattern, where specialized agents communicate through a central coordinator.\par
\par
\b A. Boutique Orchestrator (The Brain)\b0\par
- Role: Coordinates the workflow between the user and other agents.\par
- Function: Ensures every request passes through the Privacy Guardrail before reaching external sources.\par
\par
\b B. Privacy Guardrail Agent (The Shield)\b0\par
- Role: Ensures data minimization and legal compliance.\par
- Key Features:\par
  - Supports multiple privacy levels (Strict, Balanced, Open).\par
  - Handles granular consent management.\par
  - Implements the "Right to Erasure" (Forget Me) feature.\par
\par
\b C. Style Profiler Agent (The Stylist)\b0\par
- Role: Analyzes user preferences to curate recommendations.\par
- Key Features:\par
  - Positive matching (Brand, Color, Budget).\par
  - Negative Preferences: Filters out "disliked" attributes.\par
  - Scoring engine for product relevancy.\par
\par
\b D. Discovery Agent (The Researcher)\b0\par
- Role: Searches for products across a variety of retailers.\par
- Function: Normalizes data from different sources.\par
\par
\b 3. Technical Implementation\b0\par
- Language: Node.js (JavaScript)\par
- Design Pattern: Object-Oriented Agent Orchestration.\par
\par
\b 4. Conclusion\b0\par
The prototype successfully demonstrates that AI personalization does not have to come at the cost of user privacy.\par
}
